{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i --glob '\"'!.git/**'\"' 'sync|Correcting chords|section regions|Chords' README.md docs tests src reascript | sed -n '1,260p' && sed -n '1,280p' tests/test_reascript.py && sed -n '1,360p' tests/test_project.py && rg -n 'sync' tests\"","aggregated_output":"README.md:42:runs the tempo/key/sections/chords detectors, and writes the results back\nREADME.md:65:  the optional `madmom` extra (`uv sync --extra madmom`). madmom's last\nREADME.md:80:shared beat-synchronous grid the `chords` stage below aligns to.\nREADME.md:82:### Key & beat-aligned chords\nREADME.md:93:The `chords` stage detects a beat-aligned maj/min chord sequence, with every\nREADME.md:112:`<project>.vgt-chords.txt`, next to the sidecar — a plain-text timestamp +\nREADME.md:115:The `chords` stage stores two parallel chord lists: `value` (the effective,\nREADME.md:116:human-correctable chords used everywhere else — apply, the chord sheet) and\nREADME.md:135:  the optional `msaf` extra (`uv sync --extra msaf`). Like madmom above,\nREADME.md:156:`[vgt]` section regions plus a muted `[vgt] Chords` track whose text items\nREADME.md:180:## Correcting chords and sections in REAPER\nREADME.md:182:Auto-detected chords and sections are sometimes wrong, and correcting raw\nREADME.md:184:in REAPER, then run one action — `vgt sync` — to read every manual edit back\nREADME.md:187:**Chords**: edit items directly on the `[vgt] Chords` track's timeline — its\nREADME.md:200:[reascript/vgt_sync.lua](reascript/vgt_sync.lua) in REAPER's Action List and\nREADME.md:201:run it (or run `vgt sync [project.rpp]` for the same pointer from the CLI).\nREADME.md:204:- scans the `[vgt] Chords` track's items — position, length, take name — by\nREADME.md:206:  chords track vgt itself created, and writes them back as\nREADME.md:207:  `analysis.chords.value.segments` with `chords.human_verified: true`;\nREADME.md:212:- never touches `analysis.chords.detected` or `analysis.sections.detected` —\nREADME.md:216:From then on: `vgt analyze` skips the chords and sections stages\nREADME.md:218:ReaScript repaints `[vgt] Chords` and the section regions identically from\nREADME.md:226:particular, the `chords` line says whether it is only machine-detected or\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:7:local CHORDS_NAME = PREFIX .. \" Chords\"\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:327:  -- vgt_sync.lua reads those edits back into the sidecar.\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:547:        -- re-read its position so chords/sections/beats placed below land\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:575:  local chords = analysis and analysis.chords and analysis.chords.value\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:576:  local segments = type(chords) == \"table\" and (chords.segments or chords) or nil\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:578:    local chords_track = add_locked_muted_track(reaper.CountTracks(0), CHORDS_NAME)\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:581:      add_labeled_item(chords_track, reference_start + (tonumber(chord.start_seconds) or 0), reference_start + (tonumber(chord.end_seconds) or 0), tostring(chord.chord or chord.label or \"N\"), false)\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:583:    managed_tracks[#managed_tracks + 1] = chords_track\ntests/test_project.py:47:def test_sync_command_points_to_the_sync_reascript(capsys: pytest.CaptureFixture[str]) -> None:\ntests/test_project.py:48:    assert main([\"sync\", str(FIXTURE)]) == 2\ntests/test_project.py:50:    assert \"reascript/vgt_sync.lua\" in err\ndocs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:15:- detected key and beat-aligned chords as text items on a muted \"[vgt] Chords\" track,\ndocs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:36:│   • records position offset     │             │  chords → sections →       │\ndocs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:62:| Separation | **LALAL.AI API** (default — active subscription; dedicated acoustic- and electric-guitar stems, which is the one stem that must be good; async upload → split → download, cached so each song 